{
  "title": "Dua for Seeking Forgiveness Which Leads to More Knowledge & More Fortune",
  "data": "Istighfar ×400\nEvery day for two months, recite 400 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْحَىُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ الرَّحْمٰنَ الرَّحِيْمَ بَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ مِنْ جَمِيْعِ ظُلْمِىْ وَجُرْمِىْ وَاِسْرَافِىْ عَلٰى نَفْسِىْ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFIRULLAAHAL LADHEE LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAAL HAYYUL QAYYOOMUR RAHMAANAR RAHEEMA BADEE'US SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI MIN JAMEE'I ZULMEE WA JURMEE WA ISRAAFEE A'LAA NAFSEE WA ATOOBU ILAYH\nI seek the forgiveness of Allah, other than Whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting, the All-Merciful, the All-Compassionate, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, from all my wrongdoing, my transgression, and my excess against my own soul, and I turn to Him in repentance.",
  "tabs": [
    "By the Light of Your Face\nShaykh al-Tusi and other scholars recommend reciting this every day:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الْمُشْرِقِ الْحَىِّ الْبَاقِى الْكَرِيْمِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BINOORI WAJHIKAL MUSHRIQIL HAYYIL BAAQIL KAREEM\nO Allah, I ask You by the light of Your shining face, the Ever-Living, the Everlasting, the Generous,\nوَاَسْئَلُكَ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الْقُدُّوْسِ\nWA AS'ALUKA BINOORI WAJHIKAL QUDDOOS\nand I ask You by the light of Your Holy Face,\nالَّذِىْ اَشْرَقَتْ بِهِ السَّمٰوَاتُ وَانْكَشَفَتْ بِهِ الظُّلُمَاتُ\nALLADHEE ASHRAQAT BIHIS SAMAAWAATU WANKASHAFAT BIHIZ ZULUMAAT\nby which the heavens shine and the darkness is dispelled,\nوَصَلُحَ عَلَيْهِ اَمْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nWA SALUHA A'LAYHI AMRUL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nand by which the affair of the first and the last is set right,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nthat You bless Muhammad and his family\nوَاَنْ تُصْلِحَ لِىْ شَاْنِى كُلَّهُ\nWA AN TUSLIHA LEE SHA'NEE KULLAH\nand set right for me all my affairs.",
    "Sufficiency in Both Worlds\nRecite every day:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHI HASBIYALLAAHU TAWAKKALTU A'LALLAAH\nIn the name of Allah, Allah suffices me, I put my trust in Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْئَلُكَ خَيْرَ اُمُوْرِىْ كُلِّهَا\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA KHAYRA UMOOREE KULLIHAA\nO Allah, I ask You for the best of all my affairs,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ خِزْىِ الدُّنْيَا وَعَذَابِ الْاٰخِرَةِ\nWA A'OODHU BIKA MIN KHIZYID DUNYAA WA A'DHAABIL AAKHIRAH\nand I seek refuge in You from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.",
    "Hasbiyallah ×7\nRecite 7 times every day:\nحَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ رَبِّىَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nHASBIYALLAAHU RABBIYALLAAHU LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA\nAllah suffices me; Allah is my Lord; there is no god but He.\nعَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظيْمِ\nA'LAYHI TAWAKKALTU WA HUWA RABBUL A'RSHIL A'ZEEM\nIn Him I trust, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne.",
    "Daily Tasbih for a Year\nRecite every day for a whole year:\nسُبْحَانَ الدَّاۤئِمِ الْقاۤئِمِ سُبْحَانَ الْقَاۤئِمِ الدَّاۤئِمِ\nSUBHAANAD DAA'IMIL QAA'IMI SUBHAANAL QAA'IMID DAA'IM\nGlory be to the Everlasting, the Ever-Standing; glory be to the Ever-Standing, the Everlasting;\nسُبْحَانَ الْوَاحِدِ الْاَحَدِ سُبْحَانَ الْفَرْدِ الصَّمَدِ\nSUBHAANAL WAAHIDIL AHADI SUBHAANAL FARDIS SAMAD\nglory be to the One, the Unique; glory be to the Single, the Self-Sufficient;\nسُبْحَانَ الْحَىِّ الْقَيُّوْمِ سُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَبِحَمْدِهٖ\nSUBHAANAL HAYYIL QAYYOOMI SUBHAANALLAAHI WA BIHAMDIH\nglory be to the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting; glory be to Allah and with His praise;\nسُبْحَانَ الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ سُبْحَانَ الْمَلِكِ الْقُدُّوْسِ\nSUBHAANAL HAYYIL LADHEE LAA YAMOOTU SUBHAANAL MALIKIL QUDDOOS\nglory be to the Ever-Living Who never dies; glory be to the King, the Holy;\nسُبْحَانَ رَبِّ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةِ وَالرُّوْحِ سُبْحَانَ الْعَلِىِّ الْاَعْلٰى\nSUBHAANA RABBIL MALAA'IKATI WAR ROOHI SUBHAANAL A'LIYYIL A'LAA\nglory be to the Lord of the angels and the Spirit; glory be to the High, the Most High;\nسُبْحَانَهٗ وَتَعَالٰى\nSUBHAANAHOO WA TA'AALAA\nglory be to Him, and exalted is He."
  ],
  "merits": "Istighfar ×400: A tradition reported from Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) holds: He who says this imploration for Almighty Allah’s forgiveness four hundred times each day for two successive months will be granted much knowledge or much fortune.\n\nBy the Light of Your Face: Al-Tusi and other scholars have stated that it is a highly recommended tradition to say this supplication every day.\n\nSufficiency in both worlds: Al-Kaf’ami has reported Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) as saying: He who says this supplication every day, Almighty Allah will suffice him from the troubles of his two abodes (i.e. the worldly life and the Next Life).\n\nHasbiyallah ×7: It is also reported that whoever repeats this litany seven times every day, Almighty Allah will suffice him from the troubles of his two abodes.\n\nDaily tasbih: It has been also reported that whoever says these words of glorification every day for a whole year will not die before he sees (in a dream) his place in Paradise."
